From: songze <songze.cai@gl-inet.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ovpn-dco: use core-managed per-CPU stats on newer kernels

The UDP tunnel transmit helpers require a valid pcpu_stat_type on newer
kernels. Leaving it as NONE triggers iptunnel_xmit_stats warnings when
the DCO interface sends IPv4 UDP traffic.

Use the networking core's TSTATS allocation and release on Linux 6.8 and
newer. Keep the existing manual allocation and release on older kernels.
The type selection and ownership changes must stay paired to avoid
allocating the stats twice or freeing them twice.

This is a local compatibility backport, not an upstream ovpn-dco commit.

--- a/drivers/net/ovpn-dco/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ovpn-dco/main.c
@@ -41,7 +41,9 @@ static void ovpn_struct_free(struct net_device *net)
 	struct ovpn_struct *ovpn = netdev_priv(net);
 
 	security_tun_dev_free_security(ovpn->security);
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 8, 0)
 	free_percpu(net->tstats);
+#endif
 	flush_workqueue(ovpn->crypto_wq);
 	flush_workqueue(ovpn->events_wq);
 	destroy_workqueue(ovpn->crypto_wq);
@@ -134,6 +136,10 @@ static void ovpn_setup(struct net_device *dev)
 	dev->ethtool_ops = &ovpn_ethtool_ops;
 	dev->needs_free_netdev = true;
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 8, 0)
+	dev->pcpu_stat_type = NETDEV_PCPU_STAT_TSTATS;
+#endif
+
 	dev->netdev_ops = &ovpn_netdev_ops;
 
 	dev->priv_destructor = ovpn_struct_free;
--- a/drivers/net/ovpn-dco/ovpn.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ovpn-dco/ovpn.c
@@ -78,9 +78,11 @@ int ovpn_struct_init(struct net_device *dev)
 	if (!ovpn->events_wq)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 8, 0)
 	dev->tstats = netdev_alloc_pcpu_stats(struct pcpu_sw_netstats);
 	if (!dev->tstats)
 		return -ENOMEM;
+#endif
 
 	err = security_tun_dev_alloc_security(&ovpn->security);
 	if (err < 0)
